G-Mon wrote:
> James <james.kanze@gmail.com> wrote:
>
>> If you're not chaotic, killing a human has some bad side
>> effects (loss of telepathy, reduction in luck).
>
> Addendum: killing a *peaceful* human (that is, one generated peaceful, 
> e.g. a shopkeeper) as a non-chaotic costs you 5 luck and intrinsic 
> telepathy ("You murderer!"). You'll probably want a few tins of 
> floating eye meat (to get telepathy back) and a reliable way to 
> increase luck (so you can safely pray/wish) after a shopkeeper 
> murdering spree.

This is the main argument for why I don't kill many shopkeepers.  By the
time I have several tins of floating eye meat the items in shops are
getting less and less valuable to me and I have so much gold I'd rather
just spend it than deal with the costs.  By that time the number of
experience points to get to the next level is so high I'm not likely to
be able to advance by killing all of the shopkeepers in the dungeon.  By
then I'm looking for foocubi, nurses and so on not shopkeepers.  Before
I have tins of floating eye meat telepathy is too valuable for me to
waste it on killing a shopkeeper.

In comparison if the only altar I've found above Medusa is a cross
aligned mine town shrine I'll note the level of several eyes, go take
out that priest and pay the price in luck.  A co-aligned altar is worth
more than many of shops without magic lamps.  Most dungeons have altars
other than the mine town shrine, but not all dungeons.  Every so often
the next one is in the VotD (or the Quest).  Not the best of altars ...


